Feeling hyperactive mentally is a new or worsening symptom.
Feeling hyperactive physically is a new or worsening symptom.
Feeling more depressed is a new or worsening symptom.
Having thoughts about suicide is a new or worsening symptom.
Having thoughts about hurting yourself is a new or worsening symptom.
Call your doctor at once if you have:
fast or pounding heartbeats, fluttering in your chest, shortness of breath, and sudden dizziness (like you might pass out);
slow heartbeats;
unusual thoughts or behavior;
easy bruising, unusual bleeding; or
low levels of sodium in the body - headache, confusion, slurred speech, severe weakness, vomiting, loss of coordination, feeling unsteady.
Seek medical attention right away if you have symptoms of serotonin syndrome.
Symptoms of serotonin syndrome include agitation, hallucinations, fever, sweating, shivering, fast heart rate, muscle stiffness, twitching, loss of coordination, nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea.
Common trazodone side effects may include:
drowsiness, dizziness, tiredness;
swelling;
weight loss;
blurred vision;

